/plugin/ent-search/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/application/search/SearchApplicationIndexService.java-x-pack/plugin/ent-search/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/application/search/SearchApplicationIndexService.java-16408:16433-16449:16494","promptId":"#57MP3","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/ent-search/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/application/search/SearchApplicationIndexService.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/ent-search/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/application/search/SearchApplicationIndexService.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":16408,"endPos":16433,"startLine":342,"startLineOffset":40,"endLine":342,"endLineOffset":65,"length":26}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":16449,"endPos":16494,"startLine":343,"startLineOffset":40,"endLine":343,"endLineOffset":85,"length":46}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":250,"line":250,"comment_lines":["[][250]"],"review_comment":["@dakrone \r\nI found that rest yaml tests failed due to the differences in resolved index names when using security and unresolved names without security.\r\n\r\n So I added this logic with `resolvedIndices` to use the actual indices when security is not enabled. This [commit](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/106514/commits/e3d5ce57334223301c66969225a4c45f5ed61f3f) specifically.\r\n\r\nIf you think this is too messy, I\u0027d suggest we remove action information entirely from the action result, leaving only status code and optional error info. The error will still contain the missing alias name which will probably be enough info to diagnose the issue.The action information could be added back in the follow-up once this class is a bit clearer.\r\n","I think this is reasonable, thanks"],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/action/admin/indices/alias/TransportIndicesAliasesAction.java","id":35298,"created_at":"2024-04-03T17:10:49Z","original_position":93,"side":"RIGHT","position":93,"submitted_on_commit":"481ee9d8cd64812b96a7fff5d7d8f64ce4161a01"